{% comment %} 400x240 (520x390 on X) — OG has no room for the ingredient list, a count stands in
  for it there, always. X's bigger panel (screen--lg) has room to show the real list instead, but
  falls back to the same count if a recipe ever gets too long for even X's extra room — 4 is the
  most ingredients any current recipe has (Irish Coffee), so this is "show everything we have
  today, guard against a longer one later" rather than an arbitrary cutoff. Liquid renders
  identically for both screen sizes (see shared.liquid's --s scaling), so both the list and the
  count are always rendered here and shared.liquid's CSS picks which one is visible per screen
  size via the .coffee-meta--quadrant/.ingredients-fit/.screen--lg selectors.
  See full.liquid for how title_fit/count_scale work; target_w is this variant's real measured
  column width. Only div.layout + div.title_bar are authored here — TRMNL's platform injects the
  view/view--quadrant wrapper itself. {% endcomment %}
{% capture title_px_raw %}{% render "title_fit", name: name, target_w: 260, c: 0.72, min_px: 9, max_px: 20 %}{% endcapture %}
{% assign title_px = title_px_raw | strip | times: 1.5 | round %}
{% capture cs_raw %}{% render "count_scale", ingredients: ingredients %}{% endcapture %}
{% assign cs = cs_raw | strip | times: 1.0 %}
{% assign gap_px = 34 | times: cs | round %}
{% assign subtitle_px = 15 | times: cs | round %}
{% assign cup_scale = 1.6 | times: cs %}
{% assign meta_class = 'coffee-meta coffee-meta--quadrant' %}
{% if ingredients.size <= 4 %}{% assign meta_class = meta_class | append: ' ingredients-fit' %}{% endif %}
<div class="layout layout--row">
  <div class="coffee-content flex flex--row portrait:flex--col flex--center-x flex--center-y w--full h--full" style="gap:calc({{ gap_px }}px * var(--s, 1))">
    {% render "cup", ingredients: ingredients, total_ml: total_ml, scale: cup_scale %}
    <div class="{{ meta_class }}">
      <h3 class="coffee-title" style="--fs:{{ title_px }}">{{ name }}</h3>
      <div class="coffee-count" style="--fs:{{ subtitle_px }}">{{ ingredients.size }} ingredient{% if ingredients.size > 1 %}s{% endif %}</div>
      {% render "ingredient_list", ingredients: ingredients, text_size: subtitle_px %}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

